---
args: { request: RequestEnvelope, snapshot: Snapshot }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind goal = frameRequest(request). Preserve the user's exclusions and evidence standard.
2. Bind policy = selectPolicy(snapshot.policyCandidates, request.scope). Keep unresolved precedence as a blocker.
3. Bind graph = formTaskGraph(goal, snapshot), then evidencePlan = planEvidence(graph, snapshot). The plan records searched partitions and missing coverage.
4. Bind stage1 = recoverMeasures(goal, policy, snapshot.caseRecords, snapshot.evidencePages). Its candidates are the typed records frozen in the request snapshot.
5. Bind stage2 = assessComparability(goal, policy, stage1.accepted, snapshot.evidencePages). Consume only actually accepted stage1 records; carry unresolved drafts forward.
6. Bind stage3 = proposeTransforms(goal, policy, stage2.accepted, snapshot.evidencePages). Compare changes against the evidence pages and retain partial scope when justified.
7. Bind stage4 = constructCohort(goal, policy, stage3.accepted, snapshot.evidencePages). Keep dependency cycles, deduplicated reviewers, and unresolved premises explicit.
8. Bind stage5 = auditSensitivity(goal, policy, stage4.accepted, snapshot.evidencePages). Require expected-version and owner-authority evidence before a resolution delta can pass its gate.
9. Bind stageOutputs = { stage1, stage2, stage3, stage4, stage5 }. Bind collectionFindings = reconcileCollection(stageOutputs, snapshot), accounting for every candidate and cross-stage dependency.
10. Bind unresolved = { stage1: stage1.nextQuestions, stage2: stage2.nextQuestions, stage3: stage3.nextQuestions, stage4: stage4.nextQuestions, stage5: stage5.nextQuestions }. Bind reviewQuestions = resolveQuestions(unresolved, snapshot). Bind invalidation = assessDelta(snapshot, snapshot.evidencePages). Bind reviewPacket = prepareReview(stageOutputs, reviewQuestions).
11. Bind authorizedView = composeView(stageOutputs, request.requestedBy). Bind revisionProposal = proposeRevision(collectionFindings, graph). Preserve uncertainty and do not authorize an effect.
12. For each operational condition described below, inspect the supplied typed records, actor authority, dates, scope, and current versions. Carry its specific rule into the relevant named stage and the final review, view, and action proposals. Keep unsupported or conflicting conclusions unresolved. Do not invent records or claim a host-side authorization, write, delivery, or effect.
13. When supplied evidence establishes “A zero is a valid response in one study but missing in another”, apply this operational rule: preserve distinct missingness semantics. Carry the result through the existing stage outputs, unresolved questions, authorized view, revision proposal, and proposed actions as applicable; use only supported facts and keep the outcome proposed until host authorization.
14. When supplied evidence establishes “A category combines two concepts”, apply this operational rule: do not invent a finer split without evidence. Carry the result through the existing stage outputs, unresolved questions, authorized view, revision proposal, and proposed actions as applicable; use only supported facts and keep the outcome proposed until host authorization.
15. When supplied evidence establishes “A unit changes within a dataset”, apply this operational rule: bind transformations to row-level collection versions. Carry the result through the existing stage outputs, unresolved questions, authorized view, revision proposal, and proposed actions as applicable; use only supported facts and keep the outcome proposed until host authorization.
16. When supplied evidence establishes “Participant overlap exists across studies”, apply this operational rule: retain linkage uncertainty for downstream analysis. Carry the result through the existing stage outputs, unresolved questions, authorized view, revision proposal, and proposed actions as applicable; use only supported facts and keep the outcome proposed until host authorization.
17. When supplied evidence establishes “A mapping is revised”, apply this operational rule: invalidate only derived slices using that rule. Carry the result through the existing stage outputs, unresolved questions, authorized view, revision proposal, and proposed actions as applicable; use only supported facts and keep the outcome proposed until host authorization.
18. Return { caseId: request.caseId, goal, policy, graph, evidencePlan, stage1, stage2, stage3, stage4, stage5, unresolved, collectionFindings, reviewQuestions, invalidation, review: reviewPacket, view: authorizedView, revision: revisionProposal, proposedActions: stage5.proposedActions, commitAllowed: false } as the RunProposal. Host authorization, approval, persistence, and effect dispatch remain separate.
